	(text "ANALOG PI LOOP FILTER + INTEGRATOR HOLD (per channel)  |  Copy into new analog sheet / DFBLaser.\nInverting PI integrator U830 (OPA192): input Ri=R830=10k from ERR1; feedback = Ci=C830=1n in series with Rp=R831=1k (PI zero). IN+ to VREF_MID.\nIntegrator unity-gain f_i=1/(2*pi*Ri*Ci)~15.9kHz ; PI zero f_z=1/(2*pi*Rp*Ci)~159kHz. START values - final gains await measured discriminator slope (open item 5).\nOutput CORR1 -> Rsum=R832=10k -> DITH1_SUM (the existing OPA192 IN+ summing node, reused from the old dither path). This trims the DC current setpoint.\nHOLD/RESET: SW820 (SPST analog switch, e.g. ADG419) across Ci. Teensy LOCK1_EN drives it: HOLD(reset integrator) while acquiring, RUN(open) when locked. Map LOCK1_EN polarity to the chosen switch (active-high/low) - FLAG.\nFLAG: clamp/limit CORR1 authority so the summed setpoint cannot exceed 100mA / Vf (couples to the DAC->current budget). Generic op-amp pinout 1=OUT 2=IN- 3=IN+ 4=V- 5=V+."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.546 41.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c45fa29f-b52d-4a6e-a79a-6ffd575cd7fc")
	)
	(text "CONFIRMED PINS: P1=TEC+ P2=NTC_A P5=NTC_GND P10=CHIP+ P11=CHIP- P13=GND P14=TEC-"
